From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] udev: match hidraw hide rules to their HID device

A hidraw hide rule matched the kernel name alone (KERNEL=="hidraw3").
unhide_device() looks the device up before deleting its rules, so a source
that is removed (re-enumerated, unbound) leaves its rules behind, and the
next device to get that hidraw number is hidden too. On the AYANEO Pocket
VERT the controller came up as hidraw3, re-enumerated as hidraw5 during
boot, and InputPlumber's own deck-uhid target then got hidraw3: mode 000,
so Steam saw no controller until InputPlumber restarted.

Match the parent HID device as well, as the input rules match their
parent and ids. Its name carries an instance number that is new on every
enumeration (0003:4001:0428.0008), so a leftover rule cannot match another
device. SUBSYSTEM instead of SUBSYSTEMS, since udev matches all parent
keys against one device and the HID parent is in "hid".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/udev/device.rs
+++ b/src/udev/device.rs
@@ -791,9 +791,18 @@
         let match_rule = match subsystem.as_str() {
             "hidraw" => {
                 let name = self.name.clone();
-                Some(format!(
-                    r#"ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEMS=="{subsystem}", KERNEL=="{name}""#
-                ))
+                // The parent's instance number is new on every enumeration, so a
+                // stale rule cannot hide whatever reuses its hidraw number.
+                // SUBSYSTEM, not SUBSYSTEMS: udev matches all parent keys
+                // against one device.
+                match self.get_parent_device_name() {
+                    Some(parent) => Some(format!(
+                        r#"ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="{subsystem}", KERNEL=="{name}", KERNELS=="{parent}""#
+                    )),
+                    None => Some(format!(
+                        r#"ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEMS=="{subsystem}", KERNEL=="{name}""#
+                    )),
+                }
             }
